      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Context",
          "content": "An increase of bile acids (BAs), fibroblast growth factor 19 (FGF19), and glucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) has been implicated in metabolic improvements after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and vertical sleeve gastrectomy. However, data are still conflicting regarding their role after laparoscopic adjustable gastric banding (LAGB)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Objective",
          "content": "To assess the fasting BA, FGF19, and GLP-1 concentrations in plasma before and after LAGB and to test for correlations with immunometabolic parameters. Furthermore, hepatic farnesoid X receptor (FXR) expression and regulation of FXR-dependent genes were analyzed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Design and Setting",
          "content": "Observational study at the University Hospital Innsbruck."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Patients",
          "content": "Twenty obese patients."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Interventions",
          "content": "Fasting plasma samples were taken before, 3, 6, and 12 months after LAGB. Liver biopsies were obtained at surgery and after 6 months postoperatively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Main Outcome Measures",
          "content": "BA profiles, GLP-1 and FGF19 levels, hepatic FXR expression and regulation of FXR target genes were determined."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Results",
          "content": "Total, conjugated, and secondary BAs transiently increased 3 months after LAGB (P < 0.01). Only one BA, glycolithocholic acid sulfate, remained significantly elevated throughout the whole follow-up period (P < 0.05). GLP-1 had increased transiently 3 months after surgery (P < 0.01), whereas FGF19 levels increased continuously (P < 0.05). Insulin, homeostasis model assessment index, C-reactive protein, FGF19, and GLP-1 correlated positively with different BAs. No differences were seen in hepatic FXR expression and FXR-regulated genes."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Conclusions",
          "content": "Our study results, not only identified LAGB-induced changes in BAs and BA-induced hormones, but also revealed associations between changes in BA profile with GLP-1 and FGF19."
        }
      ]},
